  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAPACITY BUILDING OF CCFN ON HUMANITARIAN ASSISTANCE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will support CCFN&#x2019;s staff capacity development. The Emergency Coordinator will be trained by AMREF, Kenya on disaster preparedness and response. The course will reposition CCFN&#x2019;s preparedness to deal with emergencies and disasters in Nigeria. The capacity building would enable CCFN to carry out thorough mapping of potential threats and risks within Nigeria especially with the upcoming national elections in the first quarter of 2015. Nigerian is undergoing lots of security challenges and emergencies are imminent in such situations. Also, the general elections in Nigeria are scheduled for 2015. During the previous elections, violence has broken out which led to urban emergencies. The situation in Nigeria leading to the general elections is more precarious since there are two major parties in the country and the competition for position shall be fierce.</narrative>
  </description>
